    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d372">

                <pb facs="0340" n="320" sameAs="frus:frus1864p3/pg320"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr. Pike.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#float-left">No. 165.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-07-11"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >July</hi> 11, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to acknowledge the receipt of your
                    despatch of the 22d of June, No. 138, respecting the decline of our government
                    securities at Amsterdam, and also as to your proceedings with regard to the two
                    vessels built at Bordeaux for the rebels, and represented to have been sold to
                    certain Dutch merchants, which are approved. You will already have received
                    instructions in regard to these vessels.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">James S. Pike,</hi> Esq., <hi rendition="#italic"
                            >&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
